  "seedReflections": {
    "m01": "One forward(steps) block is better because if the flag moves I only change one number. A delivery robot would store how many metres to the next door.",
    "m02": "The loop body was forward, turn right, forward, turn left. I ran 12 instructions because 4 blocks x 3 repeats is 12. Brushing my teeth is a loop too.",
    "m03": "If you swap stop and release, the robot drops the package before it gets to the shelf. Packing my bag: check the timetable, get books, get lunch, zip it.",
    "m04": "To follow a line and stop at a box you need a light sensor for the line and a touch sensor for the box. Our classroom door uses a motion sensor.",
    "m05": "First run we turned left instead of right at C5 and hit the shelf. We traced it and fixed the turn. We went from 14 blocks to 10 with steps.",
    "m06": "We spent the most time on Test and improve because the first claw dropped the ball when it was off-centre."
  }
